[5.0, 5.5], [5.050000190734863, 5.449999809265137], [0.0, 0.4000000059604645]]}, \"flowerpot_green\": {\"asset\": \"plantsmall1\", \"asset_sha256\": \"2b9c022feb47be857b2c4fdc29f36522766ba9b70c578c31d7c05d71b4377d15\", \"position\": [8.75, 5.25, 0], \"yaw\": 0, \"uniform_scale\": 2.142857133733983, \"native_bounds\": [[-0.04733036458492279, 0.04733036458492279], [-0.04733036458492279, 0.04733036458492279], [0.0, 0.14000000059604645]], \"world_bounds\": [[8.648577690124512, 8.851422309875488], [5.148577690124512, 5.351422309875488], [0.0, 0.29999998211860657]]}}}.\nFixed IDs, source materials and native proportions must remain. ID colour suffixes are opaque names. No deletion/replacement/new object. Sizes and permitted uncertainty={\"desk_blue\": {\"size\": [1.433, 0.765, 0.75], \"size_range\": [[1.146, 0.612, 0.6], [1.72, 0.918, 0.9]]}, \"lamp_white\": {\"size\": [0.212, 0.245, 1.2], \"size_range\": [[0.17, 0.196, 0.96], [0.255, 0.294, 1.44]]}, \"plant_pink\": {\"size\": [0.259, 0.295, 0.8], \"size_range\": [[0.208, 0.236, 0.64], [0.311, 0.354, 0.96]]}, \"bin_gray\": {\"size\": [0.4, 0.4, 0.6], \"size_range\": [[0.32, 0.32, 0.48], [0.48, 0.48, 0.72]]}, \"crate_red\": {\"size\": [0.5, 0.4, 0.4], \"size_range\": [[0.4, 0.32, 0.32], [0.6, 0.48, 0.48]]}, \"flowerpot_green\": {\"size\": [0.203, 0.203, 0.3], \"size_range\": [[0.162, 0.162, 0.24], [0.243, 0.243, 0.36]]}}. Reconstructed size must use one uniform scale (nominal dimensions have 1mm rounding); height controls real mesh scale.\nFrame: x right, y back, z up, metres; position=[centre_x,centre_y,bottom_z], finite coordinates within +/-100m; yaw=0/90/180/270 degrees. Room=[4.6, 3.5, 2.5].\nInitial calibrated target views are attached after the catalogue. capture_reference obtains the actual reference. Then query_view(view) obtains one named public view; at most 2 distinct extra views. Cameras={\"reference\": {\"eye\": [2.3, -2.6671, 3.1101], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 0.35], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 320, \"height\": 240, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"front_left\": {\"eye\": [-1.1554, -1.1494, 2.9543], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 0.35], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 320, \"height\": 240, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"front_right\": {\"eye\": [5.7554, -1.1494, 2.9543], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 0.35], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 320, \"height\": 240, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"left\": {\"eye\": [-2.4205, 1.75, 2.5512], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 0.35], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 320, \"height\": 240, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"right\": {\"eye\": [7.0205, 1.75, 2.5512], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 0.35], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 320, \"height\": 240, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"top\": {\"eye\": [2.3, 1.75, 10.0667], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 1, 0]}, \"front\": {\"eye\": [2.3, -7.0667, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"side\": {\"eye\": [11.1167, 1.75, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}}. Images are real material meshes; no proxy-box input.\nSource actions use restricted Python def build(public_params): ... returning COMPLETE {id:{position:[x,y,z],yaw:0,size:[x,y,z]}}. Only room is public_params. Imports, attribute/file/network/private-task access are forbidden.\nTools: {\"tool\":\"inspect_asset\",\"id\":\"instance\"} gives an actual asset close-up at a public staging pose (no target information); {\"tool\":\"capture_reference\"}; {\"tool\":\"query_view\",\"view\":\"name\"}; {\"tool\":\"render\",\"source\":\"...\",\"view\":\"public name\"} renders your candidate; {\"tool\":\"compare\",\"source\":\"...\"} returns one mean actual-mesh silhouette IoU per acquired view only; {\"tool\":\"submit\",\"source\":\"...\"} irrevocably executes the output. No hidden acceptance/retry signal.\nAll actual mesh physical/support/room rules must hold; projected footprint needs actual upward support surfaces within 1cm; unknown intersection is not a pass. Success additionally requires hidden-camera mean per-object visible silhouette IoU >=0.8 at 160x120 actual triangle rays AND every actual bounds centre within 0.05m of the target. Hidden cameras, target transforms and hidden score are evaluator-only. No dynamics/stability simulation.\nProgram contract: Exactly one build(public_params) function, 32KiB source/64KiB JSON output. Supported: literals, assignments, arithmetic, indexing, if/else, one-generator list comprehensions (<=100 items). No for/while loops, nested functions, imports, attributes, methods, files or network. Bare callable names: range, len, min, max, abs, round, sin, cos, tan, asin, acos, atan2, sqrt, degrees, radians; pi is a fixed constant. Trigonometric inputs/outputs use radians except degrees/radians conversion. public_params contains room only.\nTurn budget: 14 actions in total including submit.  Reply with exactly one JSON object per turn and nothing else. Only the first JSON object of a reply is executed; each observation tells you how many actions remain.\nCurrent stage target observations={\"stage_views\": [{\"view\": \"front\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [2.3, -7.0667, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"capture\": {\"scene_sha256\": \"313e8e6a4048f6ef8748b81b0e0fe63fc17d5f0402a9f8794128ecec1ff8a155\", \"renders\": [{\"file\": \"reference.png\", \"sha256\": \"0ce773d892547f388c110a4d2338b2cd2db479540ab8f328242c3426975ddd16\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [2.3, -7.0667, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"raster_width\": 640, \"raster_height\": 480}]}}, {\"view\": \"side\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [11.1167, 1.75, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"capture\": {\"scene_sha256\": \"313e8e6a4048f6ef8748b81b0e0fe63fc17d5f0402a9f8794128ecec1ff8a155\", \"renders\": [{\"file\": \"reference.png\", \"sha256\": \"2b549130e35e211dbb2c91847fe4a14b51c2670364a11c9f25566e899bf950a6\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [11.1167, 1.75, 1.25], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 0, 1]}, \"raster_width\": 640, \"raster_height\": 480}]}}, {\"view\": \"top\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [2.3, 1.75, 10.0667], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 1, 0]}, \"capture\": {\"scene_sha256\": \"313e8e6a4048f6ef8748b81b0e0fe63fc17d5f0402a9f8794128ecec1ff8a155\", \"renders\": [{\"file\": \"reference.png\", \"sha256\": \"bd029fccf72121dcbc7e6ad29277f24034ed99bae865712dcecfdbf852bccf55\", \"camera\": {\"eye\": [2.3, 1.75, 10.0667], \"target\": [2.3, 1.75, 1.25], \"fov_deg\": 50, \"width\": 640, \"height\": 480, \"up\": [0, 1, 0]}, \"raster_width\": 640, \"raster_height\": 480}]}}], \"scope\": \"Actual current target RGB and public camera calibration only\"}\nAfter a target update, use newly supplied stage views to revise the preceding reconstruction. Preserve still-correct objects. Three perpendicular views are calibrated perspective images, not orthographic projections.\nProgressive installation: 2 ordered physical stages. Complete the current operation, then use commit_stage with the same program and answer fields as submit to execute and accept it. An external change follows accepted non-final stages; inspect/capture/calibrate the updated world and repair the previous solution. Final submit is for the last stage only. Commits are irreversible and do not reveal hidden correctness; use public verification before committing. All stages are privately scored and cannot be replaced by only a final scene. Total action cap: 28.",
